ut lineup FE and the same-shooter placebo on other play types is -0.0071/-0.0075, consistent with shooter-level confound.\n- observed_sample_and_power: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_verdict: artifact_found"}, {"id": "FAM:SF32", "score": 0.095, "document": "# FAM:SF32 | Study family SF32: Opener recommendations vs personnel feasibility\n- observed_research_question: Opener recommendations vs personnel feasibility\n- auto_outcome_status: artifact\n- observed_hypothesis: Rank-1 openers are within what the top-8 rotation can sustain.\n- observed_result: [APPA-033] 8/8 rank-1 openers CUT-centered and INFEASIBLE; worst gaps +9.6 to +15.9pp; CUT target 14-18% vs ceiling 2-6%.\n- observed_result: [APPM-025] All 24 openers seeded by CUT/PUTBACK/TRANSITION/PNR; CUT target exceeds stretch ceiling by +9.6 to +15.9pp for every team (e.g. PHI capacity 1.7% vs target 16.4%).\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:BASE_RATE\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: [APPA-033] Optimizer ignores personnel; CUT target 3-10x stretch ceiling in every team-game.\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF11"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-087", "score": 0.087, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-087 | Study family SF-APPS-087: Connector tangible impact: star shielding, TO, lineup lift\n- observed_research_question: Connector tangible impact: star shielding, TO, lineup lift\n- auto_outcome_status: rejected\n- observed_hypothesis: Connector presence shields stars (higher TS, lower TO) and lifts lineup ORtg beyond talent.\n- observed_result: Star dTS +0.05 pp p=0.937; dTO +0.74 pp p=0.00364 (wrong sign for shielding). Star-init TO~HasConn beta=+0.34 pp p=0.439. HasConn on-off PPP BOTH_NULL (mean -0.041 p=0.939, median +0.528 p=0.731, n=73). Frequent-conn lin [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: B